severity. Distinguish explicitly configured execution from commands derived from untrusted data. A boundary merely touched does not establish an exploit. Reserve High-to-Critical scores for demonstrated unsafe data flow or a concrete provider no-egress violation; explain the path and impact in the rationale.\n\nScore guide:\n- 0-10: no security-relevant change or clean, bounded hardening\n- 11-25: minor change near a trust boundary with no clear weakness\n- 26-50: meaningful boundary, dependency, subprocess, or CI change requiring review\n- 51-70: suspicious or weakened no-egress, sandbox, path, or supply-chain controls\n- 71-85: demonstrated unsafe input flow to execution, path access, or disclosure, or a concrete provider no-egress violation\n- 86-100: clear backdoor, provider runtime egress, credential exposure, or supply-chain compromise with a traced failure path\n\nOutput ONLY this JSON object as the final line:\n\n{\"value\": <number 0-100>, \"rationale\": \"<1-2 evidence-based sentences>\"}"
