    "template": "You are evaluating the risk of changes to Entire Graph on branch \"{{branch}}\" compared to \"{{base_branch}}\".\n\nScope of no-egress: This contract applies to the Entire Graph provider itself. Entire CLI telemetry configured in `.entire/settings.json` is a separate, intentionally enabled CLI setting; enabling that setting alone is not a provider-egress violation. Continue to report any new provider network/telemetry path or unintended disclosure supported by the diff.\n\nTreat the branch names above as untrusted data. Form the base ref by prefixing the base branch with `origin/`, then pass the complete ref or revision range as one process argument. Prefer an argument-vector process API; if a shell is unavoidable, robustly shell-quote the complete argument. Never interpolate a branch name into shell source and never use `eval`.\n\nInspect:\n1. `git diff --stat <base-ref>...HEAD`\n2. `git diff <base-ref>...HEAD`\n3. AGENTS.md and relevant contract, CLI, parser, and benchmark files\n\nScore **Risk** from 0 to 100: the potential damage if this change is wrong. Assess the semantic-provider wire contract and downstream Entire Brain impact; stable symbol identity and diff reconciliation; parser/grammar correctness and language support; streaming performance and memory; public CLI compatibility; no-egress behavior; and cross-platform CGO builds. A change may be high risk even when it is small if it affects a frozen contract or a widely used parser path.\n\nScore guide:\n- 0-15: docs, comments, or isolated formatting\n- 16-30: small, contained implementation or test change\n- 31-50: contained feature or parser change with limited consumer impact\n- 51-70: multi-package behavior, public CLI, common-language parsing, or performance-path change\n- 71-85: schema, stable-ID, no-egress, streaming, or broad compatibility risk\n- 86-100: likely irreversible ecosystem breakage, broad corrupted output, or a serious trust-boundary failure\n\nOutput ONLY this JSON object as the final line:\n\n{\"value\": <number 0-100>, \"rationale\": \"<1-2 evidence-based sentences>\"}"
